    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW22ykMMYap3WBMUhHviqhAoA?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW22ykMMYap3WBMUhHviqhAoA)_\n\nFollow-up to #24 (merged).\n\n**Before:** `emacs-pr` gave all sandboxes one shared `elpaca` folder and one shared notes copy, so only one sandbox could safely run at a time, and a sandbox could only be started from a shell.\n\n**After:**\n- Each PR gets its own `var/elpaca`, an APFS clone of a seed that is itself a clone of the live `var/elpaca`, and its own `HOME` with a clone of `~/notes` (`~/.cache/emacs-sandbox/home/pr-N`). Any number of sandboxes can run at once, next to the live Emacs. Only the native-compile cache is still shared, which Emacs supports. `emacs-pr rm N` deletes everything of a PR, `emacs-pr reset N` refreshes its notes, and `emacs-pr reseed` drops the seed.\n- A new module, `sp-sandbox`, adds `M-x sp-sandbox-pr` (the number defaults to the `22` or `#22` at point), `sp-sandbox-remove`, `sp-sandbox-reset-notes` and `sp-sandbox-reseed`. They run the fish function in a separate process from the Emacs you are working in and show its output in `*emacs-pr*`.\n- The README section \"Testing a pull request in a sandbox\" describes the new layout and the commands. Chemacs2 is not needed: `--init-directory` already gives each worktree its own packages, and the isolation comes from the per-PR `HOME` and clones, which a Chemacs2 profile would not provide.\n\n**How it was checked:** the function passes `fish -n`. I ran it against a local stand-in for the yadm repository, with stub `emacs` and `cp`, for two PRs, a re-run and `rm`. Each PR's build symlinks pointed into its own `elpaca`, each got its own home, and `rm` removed one without touching the other. The Emacs commands were run in batch against a stub `emacs-pr` (arguments, output buffer, number at point), and `sp-sandbox.org` tangles to `sp-sandbox.el` identically in Emacs 29.3. I did not run any of this with real yadm, Emacs or APFS, so the first real launch on the Mac is the test.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_015QV8A7ivyRigBtBymbF9FR)_",
